[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) was marked known, with one fix queued. It held two problems, and that
fix reached only one of them. Engineering closed #4471 on 5 October with a different outcome for
each problem, and each now has its own closed ticket.

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

The last column still says the smaller group has no ticket of its own. The table is built from the
desk's export, which does not know about the tickets below.

## The two problems

- **[Parser reads day-first dates month first](https://github.com/jacksoncarl/support-kb-4471/issues/1): fixed.**
  A day-first tenant's dates came out flipped. Engineering shipped
  `fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales`.
- **[booking-v3 hints MM/DD/YYYY to day-first tenants](https://github.com/jacksoncarl/support-kb-4471/issues/2): won't fix.**
  The form's hint told people to type the month first, and the form then read the date the tenant's
  way. The parser was not involved. Engineering retired the booking-v3 form instead of changing it.

<Callout kind="warn">
Do not report #4471 as one fixed bug. The parser fix does not cover the hint reports: they closed
because the form was retired.
</Callout>

## How to tell them apart

Use the tenant and the channel: `src/lib/kb/causes.ts` decides. A report through the booking form of a
tenant on booking-v3 is the hint problem. Every other report from a day-first tenant is the parser
problem.

Do not use these three things:

- **The subject line.** Decision 0001 merges on it, and both problems share the same subjects.
- **The intake tag.** It is a guess from the reporter's browser, and it disagrees with the tenant in
  both groups.
- **The raw row count.** The export repeats some rows, so count each report id once.

The note under the table counts reports that read as a move of one day, not a flipped date. They are
counted where the tenant files them. They do not have a ticket of their own, and the first ticket
lists them to re-check now that the parser fix has shipped.

## What this page does not change

[Decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) stays as accepted: only a new record can replace
it. The [#4471 page](/kb/incidents/4471) belongs to the desk and is unchanged, so it still says the fix
is queued.

